# DTF tier manifest: otlp-logs-metrics  (artifact-keeper#4337, fixed by #4820;
# #4931 follow-ups fixed by #4959 and #5018; 1.12.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem + telemetry.otlp-sink (OTLP/HTTP export, http/protobuf,
# to the stdlib sink harness/tiers/deps-1.12.0-controls/fixtures/otlp_sink.py,
# which counts POSTs per path and keeps their raw bodies for a grep, optionally
# restricted to one path). The profile points OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT at
# http://172.16.<slot>.71/v1/traces, the form the docs and every profile use.
# A sibling of bind-ip-and-otel, which gates spans; this tier gates logs and
# metrics. Each leg recreates only the backend with fixtures/backend.common.yml
# (2 s metric interval, 500 ms log batch delay, sqlx::query=debug) and, where
# the signals are wanted, fixtures/backend.signals.yml.
#
# THE FEATURE
# #4820 exports tracing events as OTLP log records and the metrics recorder's
# series as OTLP metrics, beside the existing span export. Both signals are
# opt in (OTEL_LOGS_EXPORTER=otlp, OTEL_METRICS_EXPORTER=otlp) and, over http,
# go to the endpoint with /v1/traces swapped for /v1/logs and /v1/metrics.
# sqlx's per-statement events never become log records (SQL text stays out of
# the collector). Exporters fail soft: a collector that is down must not slow
# startup, requests or shutdown.
#
# THE LEGS AND GATES
# Leg U, exporters unset.
#   (CONTROL) spans arrive on /v1/traces (the request's marker is in them);
#             nothing arrives on /v1/logs or /v1/metrics over 3 metric
#             intervals. Both images.
# Leg O, OTEL_LOGS_EXPORTER=otlp and OTEL_METRICS_EXPORTER=otlp.
#   (CONTROL) spans still arrive on /v1/traces with the marker. Both images.
#   (FIX)     RED on 1.11.5 (it ignores both variables; nothing but traces):
#             logs      POSTs on /v1/logs; the bodies carry "Request
#                       completed" with the X-Correlation-ID of at least 8 of
#                       the 10 requests, and "Starting Artifact Keeper". (The
#                       request's method and uri are fields of the enclosing
#                       http_request span, not of the event, and the OTel log
#                       layer exports event fields only; a record joins its
#                       span through trace_id/span_id.)
#             metrics   POSTs on /v1/metrics whose bodies carry
#                       ak_http_requests_total and
#                       ak_http_request_duration_seconds.
#             no SQL    stdout shows SQL statement text (sqlx::query=debug),
#                       yet no /v1/logs body contains SELECT, INSERT INTO,
#                       UPDATE ... SET or DELETE FROM. Requires log bodies, so
#                       it is red on 1.11.5 too.
#   (startup) the "OpenTelemetry tracing enabled" line still prints.
# Leg D, signals on, the sink container stopped (its address unreachable).
#   (GUARD)   /readyz answers within the slower of legs U and O + 15 s;
#             at least 8 of 10 requests take under 1 s and the median is
#             within leg O's median + 300 ms; `docker stop` completes within
#             25 s with a clean exit (not SIGKILL) and no panic is logged.
#             Both images (1.11.5 exports spans only, which already fail
#             soft); they guard the new exporters against a regression.
#   (FIX #4931, #5018; RED on 1.11.9, which exports no log records)
#             fields    the exported "Request completed" records carry the
#                       request's own method and uri attributes (#5018 copies
#                       them from the request because the log layer exports
#                       event fields only): method=GET, and the exact uri of at
#                       least 8 of the 10 requests. Matched as protobuf
#                       KeyValue bytes, so a span field cannot satisfy it.
#             redacted  one request with ?page=1&token=<random> is exported as
#                       uri=<path>?page=1&token=[REDACTED]; the random value
#                       is in no /v1/logs body.
#             member    a go.mod miss through a Go virtual with one local
#                       member exports artifact_keeper.virtual.member_count as
#                       the integer 1, not the string "1".
# Leg B, signals on, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT="not a url" (#4931 item 2,
#   fixed by #4959; fixtures/backend.bad-endpoint.yml).
#   (FIX)     /readyz answers, admin login works, no panic, and stderr says
#             "OTLP span export disabled". RED on 1.11.9 (the span exporter
#             panics at startup).
# Leg E, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT="" (#4931 item 3, fixed by #4959;
#   fixtures/backend.empty-endpoint.yml).
#   (FIX)     /readyz answers, no panic, and "OpenTelemetry tracing enabled"
#             does not print. RED on 1.11.9 (an empty value turns OTel on).
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: five logins across the recreates.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem telemetry.otlp-sink"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
